WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.270
- In these socially distance times,

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.890
we're always coming up with new ways

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.370
to connect with friends.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.230
One way to make sure we
stay at least six feet apart

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:10.080
is to chat car to car.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.253
That's why we created our
DRIVE-INTERVIEW, get it?

00:00:15.056 --> 00:00:17.910
♪ DRIVE-INTERVIEW ♪

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.270
Recently I had a chance, he got it.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.770
Recently I had a chance to catch up with

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.820
all around great guy, Jay Leno.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.480
I love him so much and
I got to check out a,

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.230
do an interview with him from
his car, so check it out.

00:00:31.254 --> 00:00:33.837
(upbeat music)

00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:40.346
(car engine roars)

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.160
- Hey lady.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.577
- Hey, what's up?

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:47.383
- Hi doll, how you doing?

00:00:47.383 --> 00:00:48.845
I like that Buick, how are ya?

00:00:48.845 --> 00:00:50.593
- Fancy meeting you here.

00:00:50.593 --> 00:00:51.426
- Yeah, there you go.

00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:52.874
- I liked your car,
what kinda car is that?

00:00:52.874 --> 00:00:56.100
- This is a 1970 Dodge Challenger.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.740
When I was a kid, this
is a car I always wanted

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.080
and now I got it.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.150
And I'm with the girl I always
wanted, so now I got it.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.900
So I've been doing them both for 50 years,

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.190
well I'm doing them both.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.520
That sounds terrible, doesn't it?

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.353
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:07.353 --> 00:01:08.186
That sounds bad,

00:01:08.186 --> 00:01:09.660
but you know what I mean?
- Sounds bad, sounds perfect.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:10.493
- You know what I mean?

00:01:10.493 --> 00:01:11.560
- Do you like my beauty?

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.470
- That is very nice.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:13.303
- Yeah.

00:01:13.303 --> 00:01:14.136
- That's a beautiful car.

00:01:14.136 --> 00:01:15.620
- It's Willie Nelson, blue
eyes crying in the rain.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:16.820
- I like that era more.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.030
- Yeah I know, I'm with you.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.200
Did you grow up in drive-ins?

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.030
I actually grew up around drive-in.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.240
- I did grow up around
drive-ins my first date,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.130
I remember the movie I saw was 1966,

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:29.220
the movie with The Sand Pebbles

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.590
and I took this girl, I
was trying to be very cool.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.090
You know, I remember I got some hamburgers

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.450
and the hamburger and ketchup

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:36.582
would come in with little packets.

00:01:36.582 --> 00:01:37.550
- Yeah.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.800
- So I'd reach and I do this,

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.650
you shake to get the
ketchup at the bottom.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:41.483
- Yeah.

00:01:41.483 --> 00:01:44.100
- So I'm doing that, and I
open it, I put on my burger,

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.090
very swat.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.220
I throw that back in the bag.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.610
So I'm talking to her,
I get the other Hamburg,

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:52.640
I reached out and I got another
ketchup packet, I do this.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.760
Meanwhile, I see her I go, "Ou, ou!"

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.593
I go, "What!"

00:01:56.593 --> 00:01:59.080
What I had done was I picked up the bottom

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.100
of the one I just opened,
as I was doing this,

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.980
I was throwing ketchup all over her face

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.211
and she's like, "Stop doing that,

00:02:04.211 --> 00:02:05.607
"why are you throwing Ketchup?"

00:02:05.607 --> 00:02:06.690
I go, "What!"

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.560
- And it's red, so that's awesome.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.380
- Yeah, that was pretty
much the end of the day.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.860
- It probably stained everything.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.320
I love drive-ins by the way.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.780
But did you ever have road rage?

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:16.810
Like have you ever had road rage

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.130
since you're in cars all the time?

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:20.200
- You know something,
I am a pretty calm guy.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.472
And one day, this actually
happened down here.

00:02:23.472 --> 00:02:27.200
I was on the Tonight
Show and I was somewhere

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.999
and a guy behind me.

00:02:28.999 --> 00:02:32.690
I'm like, oh, so I pull
off and I go, "Go ahead."

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.210
And as he goes by, he gives me the finger.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.470
So I wouldn't let it go and
what was that all about?

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.950
I tried, but he doesn't again.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:44.950
So now I'm really mad and I can
size up people pretty quick.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.230
So I look on him I go, let me guess,

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.960
mid fifties, bald, divorce, fat.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.427
Your kids hate you, your wife hates you.

00:02:51.427 --> 00:02:52.840
You got a dead end job.
- Oh my God I love you.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:53.710
- Your going nowhere.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.688
Your greatest day was in
high school, am I right?

00:02:55.688 --> 00:02:56.521
(indistinct)

00:02:56.521 --> 00:02:58.753
Okay, and now the guy starts crying.

00:02:58.753 --> 00:02:59.640
- Oh no.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.660
- So I'm like, "Well, I didn't mean."

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.493
He goes

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.980
I go look, so when I got out
of my car, I get in his car

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.350
and I go like, I'm
sorry, I didn't mean it.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:09.167
He goes, "No, everything
you said was right.

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:10.040
"You hit it right."

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.260
I realized I had just nailed the guy.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.153
So I said, "Well, you have a kid?"

00:03:14.153 --> 00:03:15.010
" Yes I have."

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.440
I said, "Do you have a daughter?"

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.273
and he goes, "Yes."

00:03:17.273 --> 00:03:19.437
I said, "Tailor Swift
is on the show Thursday.

00:03:19.437 --> 00:03:21.727
"I'll leave some tickets,
you bring your daughter,

00:03:21.727 --> 00:03:23.970
"I'll introduce you to
daughter to Tailor Swift."

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.040
Okay, so the guy comes
and he brings his daughter

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:26.873
and he meets her.

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:29.120
And we, and it turned
out actually very good.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.950
But it was one of those things where,

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.270
as a comedian, when you're
dealing with hecklers,

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:35.810
you can size up people pretty quick.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:36.643
- Yeah.

00:03:36.643 --> 00:03:40.400
- And I just said, fat,
bald, dead end job,

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.480
divorced.
- Divorced.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.267
- And he went, it was right on.

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:44.700
(both laughing)

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.867
I was right on, I mean, I'm not that mean,

00:03:46.867 --> 00:03:48.720
but it was right on every count.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.340
- You're almost exaggerating
and this happened.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:52.173
- Exactly.

00:03:52.173 --> 00:03:53.456
- That so nice though, what you did.

00:03:53.456 --> 00:03:55.360
- But it was funny, it was funny.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.820
- This is amazing, you're an optimist.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:58.690
- I'm an optimist,

00:03:58.690 --> 00:03:59.523
that's why.
- You are.

00:03:59.523 --> 00:04:03.210
So I had so much fun on Jay's Garage.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.050
- Yeah you did great,
people liked that a lot.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.400
We've got a lot of good reaction to it.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.650
- What's up in the new season?

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:08.990
- Well, actually we just signed today

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.294
to start our new season.

00:04:10.294 --> 00:04:11.127
So,

00:04:11.127 --> 00:04:11.960
- Oh right on.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.030
- We got a lot of celebrities lined up.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:14.590
I just can't say who just yet but--

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:15.423
- Yeah.

00:04:15.423 --> 00:04:16.810
- It's just fun, it's just a silly show

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.150
about people in cars
and doing dumb things.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.330
- I love it, yeah.

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.540
You've also got something else though.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.330
Is it you're hosting the new
version of You Bet Your Life?

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.050
- Yeah, that's still like
eight, nine months away.

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:28.050
But yeah, that'll be fun.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.640
My favorite thing when I was doing

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:31.020
the Tonight Show with Jay Walker,

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:34.270
we just went out and pick people at random

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:35.620
and ask them questions.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:36.453
- Yeah.

00:04:36.453 --> 00:04:39.520
- And I was always astounded,
you couldn't write...

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:40.777
I mean, my favorite question was,

00:04:40.777 --> 00:04:42.530
and this is an actual question.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:44.313
How was Mount Rushmore formed?

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:46.810
You know the most common answer?

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:47.643
- What?

00:04:47.643 --> 00:04:48.780
- Erosion.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:49.613
- No they did it.

00:04:49.613 --> 00:04:53.930
- Yes, I would say six out
of 10 people said erosion,

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:57.090
like the wind, the rain
picked not four presidents

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.530
but four of our greatest presidents,

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.513
just pounding the side of a mountain.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:02.783
Unbelievable.
- Wow!

00:05:02.783 --> 00:05:05.480
- I mean, if you wrote
that, people would say,

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.070
oh no, there's no one who'd ever say that,

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.090
but they did say that.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:10.310
And that's what made it
fun, when you catch people.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.530
- Or scary, fun or scary.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.180
- Yeah, or scary, yeah.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.013
- Who's out there?

00:05:15.013 --> 00:05:16.390
- I like to go with fun.

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:17.479
- Okay, yeah you're the optimist,

00:05:17.479 --> 00:05:18.312
- Exactly.

00:05:18.312 --> 00:05:19.285
I'll be the realist.
- Exactly.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.118
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:20.118 --> 00:05:20.951
Exactly.

00:05:20.951 --> 00:05:21.960
All right, well oh my gosh.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.930
I love seeing you here.

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:24.763
- It's good seeing you.

00:05:24.763 --> 00:05:26.610
- This is so awesome, next time we'll be,

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:28.180
I'll be on your show again
and we'll be on another car.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.360
- Let's do it all right, babe.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.360
- Okay, bye!

00:05:31.322 --> 00:05:32.155
- See you later.

00:05:32.155 --> 00:05:33.613
- Sounds good.

00:05:33.613 --> 00:05:36.196
(upbeat music)

